  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_001, acc=0.725) uses scvi_n200 as RNA encoder with imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion. The fusion choice (weighted vs concat) showed negligible difference (0.725 vs 0.721), and multimodal clearly outperforms RNA-only (0.725 vs 0.653). However, the RNA encoder dimension is completely unexplored—no experiment has tested scgpt or pca_n2000 in the multimodal setting. Question: config_034 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is a clean single-variable swap of the RNA encoder from scvi_n200 to scgpt while holding all other proven settings constant. This directly tests whether a generative-pretrained RNA model captures cell-state information better than the variational scvi model. Why this is the best use: The RNA encoder is the primary signal source for cellular profiling and is the highest-impact untested dimension. With 6 experiments remaining, resolving whether scgpt outperforms scvi_n200 will either confirm the current encoder (focusing future budget on other axes) or open a new promising branch, making it the highest-information-value experiment at this stage."
